=====================
AVONE PACKAGE OVERVIEW
=====================

Package:
  avone

Purpose:
  - Main AV.ONE robot package
  - Holds the robot description (URDF/Xacro), Gazebo worlds and models, RViz configs, and core launch files
  - Provides simulation bringup and basic robot sanity tests
  - Contains core C++ nodes for vehicle hardware integration (CAN and system hardware)

Where it lives:
  ~/ros2_ws/src/avone


Directory Breakdown:

• config/
  - Controller config and RViz config

  Files:
    ackermann_drive_controller.yaml
      - ros2_control controller config for Ackermann steering and joint_state_broadcaster

    view_avone.rviz
      - RViz view preset for AV.ONE (TF, RobotModel, fixed frame, etc.)


• description/
  - Robot model definition built from modular Xacro files
  - This is the single source of truth for the TF tree, link geometry, and ros2_control setup

  Key files:
    robot.urdf.xacro
      - Top-level robot entry point (xacro processed into robot_description)

    robot_core.xacro
      - Main links and joints definition, includes chassis and core frames

    inertial_macros.xacro
      - Helper macros for inertia and mass definitions

    sensors.xacro
      - Sensor frames and mounts

    camera.xacro
      - Camera frame definition

    rgbdcamera.xacro
      - RGBD camera frame definition (D435 style)

    lidar.xacro
      - LiDAR frame definition

    ros2_control.xacro
      - GazeboSimSystem ros2_control config for simulation

    ros2_control_hardware.xacro
      - Real hardware ros2_control config (CAN based), used on the physical car

  assets/
    - Meshes and visuals for the robot (STL/DAE/etc.)


• launch/
  - All ROS 2 launch entry points for sim, bringup, and subsystem testing

  Key launch files (from your tree and the code you sent):

    avone_sim.launch.py
      - Full simulation bringup
      - Gazebo world + spawn robot + ros2_control + bridges + EKF/navsat + teleop + optional RViz

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_sim.launch.py

    avone_test_sim.launch.py
      - Minimal "spawn test" in an empty world
      - Gazebo + spawn + robot_state_publisher only

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_test_sim.launch.py

    avone_rsp.launch.py
      - Desktop URDF and TF sanity test
      - robot_state_publisher + joint_state_publisher_gui + RViz config

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_rsp.launch.py use_sim_time:=false

    avone_nuc_boot.launch.py
      - NUC boot bringup style launch
      - Starts CAN DBC bridge, LED matrix state display, heartbeat, and timeout monitoring

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_nuc_boot.launch.py

    avone_control_bringup.launch.py
      - Control stack bringup (controller_manager and controllers)
      - Used when driving simulated or real hardware (depends on your setup)

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_control_bringup.launch.py

    avone_nav2_bringup.launch.py
      - Nav2 bringup for autonomy navigation

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_nav2_bringup.launch.py

    avone_localisation_bringup.launch.py
      - Localisation bringup wrapper (EKF, navsat_transform, TF helpers)

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_localisation_bringup.launch.py

    avone_gps_bringup.launch.py
      - GPS driver and related transforms (depending on your setup)

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_gps_bringup.launch.py

    avone_imu_bringup.launch.py
      - IMU bringup and transforms

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_imu_bringup.launch.py

    avone_lidar_bringup.launch.py
      - LiDAR bringup and transforms

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone avone_lidar_bringup.launch.py

    teleop_joy.launch.py
      - Joystick teleop pipeline (joy + teleop_twist_joy + filters)

      Command:
        ros2 launch avone teleop_joy.launch.py


• worlds/
  - Simulation worlds and Gazebo models


• src/
  - C++ nodes for vehicle integration and hardware interfaces

  Files:
    avone_can_interface.cpp
      - CAN interface layer (SocketCAN style)
      - Typically used to send and receive vehicle messages

    avone_system_hardware.cpp
      - ros2_control hardware interface for the real vehicle
