AVONE_MAPPING PACKAGE OVERVIEW
============================

Package:
  avone_mapping

Purpose:
  - Mapping and track understanding tools for AV.ONE
  - Processes perception outputs into usable track features (cones, boundaries, centreline)
  - Provides clustering and planning helpers used for cone based navigation
  - Includes LiDAR preprocessing utilities for cleaner cone extraction

Files:

• coloured_cone_clustering.py
  - Groups cone detections into stable cone objects,
  - Reduces noise by merging nearby detections and maintaining consistent IDs/positions over time
  - Outputs clustered cone positions for planning and visualisation

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_mapping coloured_cone_clustering

• delaunay_planner.py
  - Builds a centreline/drive path from left and right cone boundaries using Delaunay triangulation
  - Produces a smoothed midline or waypoint set suitable for a downstream controller / Nav2 style follower
  - Useful for skidpad and trackdrive style cone courses where boundaries are defined by coloured cones

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_mapping delaunay_planner

• lidar_groundremoval.py
  - LiDAR preprocessing node that removes ground points to isolate obstacles/cones
  - Improves downstream clustering reliability by reducing flat ground returns and noise
  - Typically runs before cone clustering if you are extracting cones directly from point clouds

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_mapping lidar_groundremoval

