AVONE_NAV PACKAGE OVERVIEW
=========================

Package:
  avone_nav

Purpose:
  - Main Nav2 bringup package for AV.ONE
  - Owns the Nav2 configuration, behaviour tree selection, and launch entrypoint
  - Adds AV.ONE specific glue nodes around Nav2 for track testing workflows:
    - CAN based goal start and cancel control
    - LiDAR collision detection that can trigger a CAN safety message when an object is detected ahead


Files:


• nav2_cancel.py
  - AV.ONE Nav2 goal control helper
  - Allows starting and cancelling Nav2 goals from CANBUS derived commands
  - Used to integrate external safety/state systems (RES, AMI, Teensy, etc.) with Nav2 action control

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_nav nav2_cancel

• collision_detection.py
  - Simple LiDAR based collision detection
  - Monitors points/obstacles in front of the vehicle and triggers a CAN message if an object is detected
  - Intended as a conservative safety layer during testing (independent of planner behaviour)

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_nav collision_detection


Behaviour Trees (behaviour_trees/)

• avone_bt.xml
  - AV.ONE custom Nav2 behaviour tree
  - Defines the navigation flow, replanning, and recovery logic used for AV.ONE testing

• navigate_through_poses_w_replanning_and_recovery.xml
  - Standard Nav2 behaviour tree 
  - Used for multi waypoint style navigation workflows


Config 

• nav2_config.yaml
  - Nav2 parameters for AV.ONE
  - Includes controller, planner, costmaps, lifecycle manager, and behaviour tree configuration


Launch 
• nav2.launch.py
  - Main launch file for AV.ONE Nav2 bringup
  - Starts Nav2 using avone_nav/config/nav2_config.yaml and selects the desired behaviour tree

  Command:
    ros2 launch avone_nav nav2.launch.py


===========================
AVONE_UTILS PACKAGE OVERVIEW
===========================

Package:
  avone_utils

Purpose:
  - Misc utility nodes used across the AV.ONE stack
  - Small safety and glue layers that sit between major subsystems
  - Includes:
    - cmd_vel filtering between Nav2 and the Ackermann controller
    - drive state LED output to the ESP32 matrix
    - ROS command heartbeat outputs for LVD safety monitoring
    - simple watchdog style timeout handling for sensors/inputs


Files:

• cmd_vel_filter.py
  - Safety and sanity layer between Nav2 cmd_vel and the Ackermann steering controller input
  - Holds or suppresses steering commands until a valid forward linear velocity is present
  - Prevents "steer while stationary" behaviour and reduces unwanted wheel scrubbing or oscillation

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_utils cmd_vel_filter

• drive_state_led.py
  - Publishes the current drive/state indicator to the ESP32 LED matrix
  - Used to show the vehicle state as a colour or pattern for quick visibility during testing/scrutineering

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_utils drive_state_led

• ros_cmd_heartbeat.py
  - Sends ROS derived safety heartbeats intended for the LVD
  - Used as a "system alive / autonomy alive" style signal alongside other safety layers

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_utils ros_cmd_heartbeat

• sensor_timeout.py
  - Simple watchdog that monitors critical topics for dropouts or stale data
  - Can raise a fault, publish a status, or trigger a safety output when inputs stop updating

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_utils sensor_timeout


